What this licence covers

The licence above covers this project's own work: the tools (tools/, except as
listed below), the PC port's own code (port/, except port/game/), the build
files (Makefile,
configs/), the tests and the documentation (README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
CLAUDE.md, docs/).

It does not cover:

- src/, include/ and port/game/: the decompiled C and headers, and the PC port's
  copy of them, reconstruct Crash Bash, a
  game whose code and data belong to their respective owners (developed by
  Eurocom, published by Sony Computer Entertainment). That includes the
  original game headers recovered from the game's own archive
  (include/bash/arkenoid.h, pogo.h, polar.h, tank.h). Nothing here grants any
  right to the game.
- tools/reference/: the source of GCC 2.8.1 and 2.7.2.3, under the GNU General
  Public License (the COPYING files there).
- tools/cc1/patches/: changes to GCC, under the GNU General Public License as
  GCC is.

The repository holds no game files, no SDK files and no compiler binaries. A
build needs your own copy of the game and of Sony's PsyQ SDK (README.md).
